From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bullhead-linux <kaiwalyakhasnis57@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:17:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: msm.allow_vram_carveout also lets users submit

Without an IOMMU, GPU submits are taken from CAP_SYS_RAWIO only, as the GPU
reaches all of memory. With msm.allow_vram_carveout=1 the GPU is already run
that way on purpose (MSM8992: the A418's SMMU belongs to TrustZone, no
driver), and a desktop session (Lomiri, its apps) runs as a normal user:
there, take their submits too.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c
index c0b4a346e..d0204a961 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 
 #include "msm_drv.h"
 #include "msm_gpu.h"
+#include "adreno/adreno_gpu.h"
 #include "msm_gem.h"
 #include "msm_gpu_trace.h"
 
@@ -679,7 +680,12 @@ int msm_ioctl_gem_submit(struct drm_device *dev, void *data,
 	if (args->pad)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (unlikely(!ctx->aspace) && !capable(CAP_SYS_RAWIO)) {
+	/*
+	 * Without an IOMMU the GPU reaches all of memory: only CAP_SYS_RAWIO may
+	 * submit, unless msm.allow_vram_carveout=1 already opted out of that.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(!ctx->aspace) && !allow_vram_carveout &&
+	    !capable(CAP_SYS_RAWIO)) {
 		DRM_ERROR_RATELIMITED("IOMMU support or CAP_SYS_RAWIO required!\n");
 		return -EPERM;
 	}
-- 
